@ray9368 Count me among those excited for the more modern Tombstone (more compact, brushless weapon motor, wheel guards). I'll be in Vegas to see you fight, so excited! 

I did have a question. From your previous video, the weapon bar went went down from 33 inch to 26 inch in length, and so I assume it went from 1 inch to 1.25 inch thick, to maintain the same weight (and hence kinetic energy storage). I realize this won't be in play for this tournament, but for the future do you think you might consider a weapon bar option that would be single toothed with a 10 inches of reach (so effectively a 20 inch bar if it were symmetrical), at 1.5 inches thick (for similar weight), specifically as an option for fighting vertical spinners?

It seems to me (very back of the envelope calculations) such a bar would give you a weapon that would still outreach a vertical spinner (Witch Doctor, for example, has about 7 inches of reach, which is a fairly large diameter vert). But relative to a 26 inch symmetrical bar, you would store similar kinetic energy assuming the same tip speed (slight loss as the MOI from the counterweight isn't as high), increase the tooth engagement by about 50%, and reduce the chance of a vert getting a weapon hit on the bar by about 35% in a weapon in weapon collision. Plus, the thicker bar with a shorter lever arm distance would increase its durability. Is that something that could be on the cards one day?
